  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/mumbai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mumbai</a>: Paras Healthcare reported a 22.8 per cent year on year (YoY) increase in revenue from operations to Rs 510.9 crore in the second quarter ended September, 2026.Ebitda grew 42.5 per cent YoY to Rs 126.6 crore, while PAT jumped 3.3 times to Rs 40.4 crore as compared to Rs 12.4 crore last year with PAT margin improving to 7.8 per cent from 2.7 percent.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>New hospitals at Srinagar and Kanpur more than doubled revenue in Q2 YoY to Rs 84.4 crore, with ebitda at 18.7 per cent marginIn the first half of FY27, revenue grew to Rs 981.2 crore, up 25.1 per cent YoY. PAT was at Rs 90.0 crore, up 7.9x YoY.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>Bed occupancy rose to 73.0% in from 59.0% in H1 FY26 and  ARPOB was at Rs 48.9 k.Dr. Dharminder Kumar Nagar, Managing Director, Paras Healthcare Limited, said, “Our newer hospitals at Srinagar and Kanpur have ramped up rapidly and turned strongly Ebitda positive, while our mature hospitals continue to deliver industry leading margins. Out of the IPO proceeds of Rs 500 crore, we deployed Rs 375 crore towards part repayment of our borrowings making our balance sheet significantly stronger. We will continue to deepen our specialty programmes including oncology, cardiac, neuro and renal sciences, invest in advanced clinical technology and expand our presence in the under served markets of North India.\"</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->                    <!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Nov 6, 2026 at 07:42 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Nov 6, 2026 at 07:42 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-s